}}

==Enemy==
A classy seal who attacks quickly, endures attacks without flinching and deals decent damage. It is recommended to use defensive Cats in tandem with fast-hitting ranged units to defeat this enemy.

==Strategy==
Sir Seal could be very difficult or very easy depending on how you use your cats. The first time you meet Sir Seal is in [[Greece (Empire of Cats)|Greece/Shiga]], where [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cat]] will come in handy ([[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] is even better!). Also use [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]] to make quick work of Sir Seal. You should summon lots of [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cats]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]], so that Sir Seal doesn't get to your attackers. Don't use [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]], as he gets outranged and can't take many hits.

Some time later on in [[Stories of Legend]], Sir Seal's strength magnification will fluctuate a lot and give him generally higher strength magnifications than the other enemies from Empire of Cats (i.e. [[Angry Fighting]]), so use strong anti-Reds such as Island Cat, [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] and [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sexy Bathtub Cat]] or even [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]].

Sir Seal is especially vulnerable to the Freeze effect because with one knockback he can't actually escape stunlock, and the slow-hitting but powerful characteristic of a typical [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] or [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] unit comes in handy against Sir Seal too. His above-average money drop enables you to also exploit [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|cats with Money Up abilities]] to greatly ease cash-tight stages.

