==Existence Elsewhere==
===Nyanko Daibōsō===
Sir Seal appeared as a regular enemy in [[Nyanko Daibōsō]].

===Nyanko Defence Force===
While Sir Seal himself only appeared as a stone statue in [[Nyanko Defence Force]], he had many new variants that could be fought as bosses or Raid Bosses. They had the ability to split into two smaller seals, which would then split into two even smaller seals. Some units had an ability called Sir Seal Killer, which increased damage against all seal variants by 50%.

{{Gallery|Enemy icon 008}}

==Trivia==
*He was known as "Sir Baby Seal" in [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|the old English version]].
*His Japanese name, Goma-sama (ゴマさま), is derived from ''gomafuazarashi'' (ゴマフアザラシ, "[[wikipedia:Spotted seal|spotted seal]]") and ''-sama'' (さま), an honorific which shows great respect and is mainly used for those of higher status.
*His Japanese description's mention of his coming to Tokyo out of admiration for a more popular seal references the famous seal [[wikipedia:Tama-chan|Tama-chan]].
*Sir Seal and [[Cerberus Kids]] have opposite Japanese descriptions. Sir Seal dyed himself [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] after coming to Tokyo, while Cerberus Kids were Red until they came to Tokyo.
*One of the possible endings for [[Gamatoto Expedition]] log messages is "when Sir Seal attacked!"

